[38;5;231m⏺[39m I've opened three layout sketches in a browser tab. If it didn't open on its own, the full URL is:

  [94m]8;id=agr7sz;http://localhost:52205/?key=a626ec50c9384fefe42cb06630d601dfd8d88890f2b991e083e01c4ba8d11578\http://localhost:52205/?key=a626ec50c9384fefe42cb06630d601dfd8d88890f2b991e083e01c4ba8d11578[39m]8;;\

  (The companion uses a lot of tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal.)

  All three options use the same four groups for the 12 current fields:
  - [1mProfile:[0m display name, email, avatar URL
  - [1mPreferences:[0m time zone, language, theme
  - [1mNotifications:[0m email, push, weekly digest
  - [1mSecurity:[0m two-factor auth, session timeout, API token

  The three options:
  - [1mA. Stacked sections:[0m headed groups on one page. Every field stays visible and there's still one Save button. I
    recommend this one.
  - [1mB. Tabs:[0m one group shows at a time. The page is shortest, but fields on other tabs are hidden, and switching tabs
    needs some new JavaScript.
  - [1mC. Sidebar plus sections:[0m stacked sections with jump links down the side. It needs a wider page, which is more than
    12 fields call for.

  Why I recommend A: only [38;5;153msettings.html[39m and [38;5;153msettings.css[39m change, every field keeps its name, and the data [38;5;153msettings.js[39m
  sends to the server stays exactly the same. You can switch to tabs later without redoing the grouping.

  Which layout do you want? Is the grouping right? You can click an option in the browser too. I won't change any code
  until you approve the design.

  One more thing: the mockups are saved in [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m in this repo. You'll probably want to add it to [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m.

